  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Parvendra Singh vs State Of U.P. on 28 August, 2019 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth",
    "facts": "False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 28.7.2019, who is not a previous convict.",
    "arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, the Court is of the view that the applicant has made out a case for bail. Let the applicant, Parvendra Singh involved in Case Crime No. 239 of 2019, under Sections- 60-A, 63 of U.P. Excise Duty/ Excise Act & Section 272 I.P.C., Police Station- Haldaur, District- Bijnor, be Parvendra Singh vs State Of U.P. on 28 August, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/64423278/ 1 released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned subject to following conditions.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, the Court is of the view that the applicant has made out a case for bail. Let the applicant, Parvendra Singh involved in Case Crime No. 239 of 2019, under Sections- 60-A, 63 of U.P. Excise Duty/ Excise Act & Section 272 I.P.C., Police Station- Haldaur, District- Bijnor, be Parvendra Singh vs State Of U.P. on 28 August, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/64423278/ 1 released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned subject to following conditions."
  },
